e  and memory subtype many studies are also  identifying markers of inflammation for  example  inflammatory monocytes are have  significant morphological and functional  changes with co-19  infection and have been shown to be  involved  in proper in progression of the disease  several studies are demonstrating the  importance of tsl  exhaustion markers such as tim3 and pd1  as well as increased cd8 expression  and t cell activation marker  along with impacts on the immune cell  populations people are also studying the  immune response  mechanisms and several very interesting  publications of late  have shown study details where pbmcs are  stimulated with viral antigens  and the consequent impact on the immune  cells are being evaluated  these kind of studies not only  characterize the immune cell response  but also  look at secreted cytokines and  intracellular cytokine measurements  are also being performed and these kind  of approaches are again very important  and  vaccine development strategies as well  as drug development approaches  another big area of research a study is  evaluating viral entry  and infection mechanisms people are  interested in  how the virus is interacting with  certain cell types uh they are creating  in vitro model to understand  uh the viral mode of entry and infection  uh to understand what kind of protein  and expression markers are involved  and how these are impacted by viral  binding and  infection and drug screening and  repurposing studies  are also being extensively performed to  identify  effective antiviral strategies by taking  where people  are taking existing approved drugs  and then applying them to viral  infectivity studies and several papers  discussed in the these approaches as  shown on the right  at luminex we offer a range of platforms  and solutions  that can enable cytometry and provide  information in kobit 19 research  these include our platforms based on  microcapillary  cytometry such as the guava mu cell  analyzer and the guava side platforms  are shown on the left  and our range of imaging flow  psychometry platforms  which combine the power of imaging along  with flow cytometry  and can provide unique insights into  studies such as inflammatory  mechanisms of covid19s during this talk  i will be mainly focusing on  microcapillary flow cytometry  and my colleague dr haley pugsley will  will discuss imaging flow cytometry  so let's first take a look at what we  mean  by microcapillary cytometry  microcapillary cytometry which is shown  on your left  differs from traditional flow cytometry  on the right  shown on your right that it in in that  it does not utilize sheet fluid and  instead  the sample is aspirated directly from a  tube or a valve  through a microcapillary flow cell and  interrogated by a laser  and data is collected from detection  channels as it flows through  the simplification of fluidics results  in a more compact system  and these which are easy to operate and  need minimal maintenance  microcapillary cytometry gives rise to  some distinct advantages  first because of the nature of the  technology and the use of a precision  pop  we can get absolute cell count  information  without having to add external beads and  this capability to get absolute cons  automatically brings benefits in many  application  types the design leads to small  cellular samples being needed for  analysis and this can be very valuable  in cover 19 research where researchers  are trying to maximize the information  from precious samples available the lack  of sheath fluid  also leads to low biohazardous waste  generation  which is again highly advantageous when  dealing with  infectious samples so let's take a  closer look  at our two platforms based on  microcapillary cytometry  the guava mu system and the guava easy  size system both of which  are based on microcapillary cytometry  so the guava news cell analyzer is an  easy to use simple and compact  instrument for cell analys